IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lrnt-dates`
IMPORT `lrnt-survival`

-- Law Reform (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1956 (NT), Part II -- worked cases for the survival questions.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted from an unofficial copy under
-- the NT copyright policy of 8 October 1996 and the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names for the facts and the answers used below`

`27 Jun 1956` MEANS `the calendar date` 27 6 1956
`28 Jun 1956` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 6 1956
`1 Jun 2005` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 2005
`6 Nov 2007` MEANS `the calendar date` 6 11 2007
`7 Nov 2007` MEANS `the calendar date` 7 11 2007
`1 Jan 2020` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 2020
`29 Feb 2020` MEANS `the calendar date` 29 2 2020
`1 Mar 2020` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2020
`27 Feb 2023` MEANS `the calendar date` 27 2 2023
`28 Feb 2023` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2023
`31 May 2023` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 5 2023
`1 Jun 2023` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 2023
`29 Feb 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 29 2 2024
`15 Mar 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 3 2024
`1 Jun 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 6 2024
`1 Jul 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 7 2024
`15 Aug 2024` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 8 2024
`1 Jan 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 1 2025
`1 Feb 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 2 2025
`28 Feb 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2025
`15 Mar 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 3 2025
`15 Aug 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 8 2025
`16 Aug 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 16 8 2025
`1 Sep 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 9 2025
`30 Nov 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 30 11 2025
`1 Dec 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 12 2025
`2 Dec 2025` MEANS `the calendar date` 2 12 2025
`7 Nov 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 7 11 2026

`HAD` MEANS `a claim the dead person had against someone else (it would benefit the estate)`
`AGAINST` MEANS `a claim someone has against the dead person (it would be brought against the estate)`
`OTHER CLAIM` MEANS `anything else (negligence, other torts, contract, a claim under the Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act 1974 and so on)`

`SURVIVES FOR` MEANS `yes: it survives for the benefit of the dead person's estate (s 5(1)); the executor or administrator may bring or continue it, with damages limited by s 6`
`SURVIVES AGAINST` MEANS `yes: it survives against the dead person's estate (s 5(1)); proceedings in tort must meet s 7`
`SURVIVES BY S 8` MEANS `yes: s 8 treats it as having existed against the person before their death, so it survives against the estate (s 5(1), s 8); proceedings in tort must meet s 7`
`EXCEPTED` MEANS `no: claims for defamation, seduction, inducing a spouse to leave or stay apart, and adultery damages do not survive under s 5 (s 5(2), the text's no)`
`DIED BEFORE 1956` MEANS `Part II does not reach it: the death was before 28 June 1956 (NOTHING-kind)`
`NO CAUSE AT DEATH` MEANS `Part II does not reach it: no cause of action existed at the death (NOTHING-kind)`

`DUST YES` MEANS `yes: the estate keeps damages for pain and suffering, bodily or mental harm and curtailment of expectation of life (s 6(2))`
`DUST YES BY 6(3)` MEANS `yes: s 6(3) extends s 6(2) to this action, which was still undetermined on 7 November 2007 though the plaintiff had died before then; the estate keeps those damages`
`DUST NOT NEEDED` MEANS `the rule is not needed: the death was not caused by the wrong, so s 6(1)(c)(ii) does not exclude those damages`
`NOT A DUST DISEASE` MEANS `no: the condition is not a dust disease (a pathological condition of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum attributable to dust) (s 6(4), the text's no); s 6(1)(c)(ii) excludes those damages`
`DUST IF FAILS` MEANS `no: s 6(2) needs the person to have commenced the action themselves, to have died as a result of the disease, and to have died before the action was determined (the text's no: its "if" fails); s 6(1)(c)(ii) excludes those damages`
`DUST DETERMINED BEFORE 2007` MEANS `no: the person died before 7 November 2007 and the action had been determined before that day (s 6(3), the text's no); s 6(1)(c)(ii) excludes those damages`

`TORT` MEANS `a claim in tort (negligence, trespass, nuisance and so on)`
`FATAL INJURIES` MEANS `a claim under the Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act 1974`
`CONTRACT` MEANS `another kind of claim (contract, debt and so on)`

`PENDING` MEANS `yes: proceedings against the person were pending when they died (s 7(1)(a))`
`TAKEN IN TIME` MEANS `yes: you took proceedings in time, within 12 months after the grant of probate or administration or the further period the Supreme Court allowed (s 7(1)(b))`
`STILL IN TIME` MEANS `still in time: you have not yet taken proceedings, and the last day (12 months after the grant, or the further period allowed) has not passed (s 7(1)(b))`
`NOT BEGUN` MEANS `still in time: probate or letters of administration have not been taken out, so the 12 months has not begun (s 7(1)(b))`
`OUT OF TIME` MEANS `out of time (s 7(1)(b), the text's no): the Supreme Court may still allow a further period, on an application made before or after the period ends`
`AROSE TOO EARLY` MEANS `no: the cause of action arose more than 12 months before the death and the court is not satisfied it is reasonable to let the proceedings continue (s 7(1)(b), s 7(2), the text's no)`
`NO S 7 CONDITION` MEANS `s 7 sets no condition: the claim is not in tort or under the Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act 1974 (NOTHING-kind); other limitation laws still apply`

§ `s 5 and s 8 -- does the claim survive the death`

-- An injured person's negligence claim, death in 2020: survives for the estate.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does the claim survive the death` `1 Jan 2020` `HAD` `OTHER CLAIM` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `SURVIVES FOR`
-- Death the day before commencement (edge).
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does the claim survive the death` `27 Jun 1956` `HAD` `OTHER CLAIM` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `DIED BEFORE 1956`
-- Death on the commencement day: "after the commencement" (edge, fork F1).
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does the claim survive the death` `28 Jun 1956` `HAD` `OTHER CLAIM` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `SURVIVES FOR`
-- The four exceptions of s 5(2), each way.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does the claim survive the death` `1 Jan 2020` `HAD` `defamation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `EXCEPTED`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does the claim survive the death` `1 Jan 2020` `AGAINST` `seduction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `EXCEPTED`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does the claim survive the death` `1 Jan 2020` `HAD` `inducing one spouse to leave or remain apart from the other` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `EXCEPTED`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does the claim survive the death` `1 Jan 2020` `AGAINST` `damages on the ground of adultery` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `EXCEPTED`
-- An excepted kind with a death before 1956: the date is checked first.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does the claim survive the death` `27 Jun 1956` `HAD` `defamation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `DIED BEFORE 1956`
-- A claim against the dead wrongdoer.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does the claim survive the death` `1 Jan 2020` `AGAINST` `OTHER CLAIM` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `SURVIVES AGAINST`
-- s 8: the wrongdoer died before the damage was suffered (a defect they built injures someone later).
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does the claim survive the death` `1 Jan 2020` `AGAINST` `OTHER CLAIM` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `SURVIVES BY S 8`
-- No cause of action at the death, and s 8 not met.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does the claim survive the death` `1 Jan 2020` `AGAINST` `OTHER CLAIM` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `NO CAUSE AT DEATH`
-- s 8 is only for claims against the dead person.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- does the claim survive the death` `1 Jan 2020` `HAD` `OTHER CLAIM` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `NO CAUSE AT DEATH`

§ `s 6(2) to (4) -- dust disease`

-- Mesothelioma: action commenced, died of it on 1 March 2020, not yet determined.
#ASSERT `s 6(2) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `1 Mar 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS `DUST YES`
-- Death not caused by the wrong: the exclusion never arose.
#ASSERT `s 6(2) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `1 Mar 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS `DUST NOT NEEDED`
-- Not of the lungs, pleura or peritoneum; not attributable to dust.
#ASSERT `s 6(2) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `1 Mar 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS `NOT A DUST DISEASE`
#ASSERT `s 6(2) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `1 Mar 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS `NOT A DUST DISEASE`
-- The estate, not the person, commenced the action.
#ASSERT `s 6(2) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `1 Mar 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS `DUST IF FAILS`
-- Died of something else.
#ASSERT `s 6(2) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE `1 Mar 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS `DUST IF FAILS`
-- Died on the day the action was determined: not "before" (edge, fork F2).
#ASSERT `s 6(2) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `1 Mar 2020` TRUE `1 Mar 2020` EQUALS `DUST IF FAILS`
-- Died the day before determination (a leap day).
#ASSERT `s 6(2) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `29 Feb 2020` TRUE `1 Mar 2020` EQUALS `DUST YES`
-- Died on the commencement day of s 6(2), undetermined.
#ASSERT `s 6(2) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `7 Nov 2007` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS `DUST YES`
-- Died the day before, undetermined: s 6(3).
#ASSERT `s 6(2) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `6 Nov 2007` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS `DUST YES BY 6(3)`
-- Died 2005; action determined on 7 November 2007 itself: still undetermined at that date (edge, fork F3).
#ASSERT `s 6(2) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `1 Jun 2005` TRUE `7 Nov 2007` EQUALS `DUST YES BY 6(3)`
-- Died 2005; determined 6 November 2007.
#ASSERT `s 6(2) -- does a dust-disease claim keep its damages for pain and suffering` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `1 Jun 2005` TRUE `6 Nov 2007` EQUALS `DUST DETERMINED BEFORE 2007`

§ `s 6(1) -- what the estate can recover`

-- Inputs: death caused, breach of promise, damage from breach, up to death, non-economic, earnings after death, loss
-- from death, funeral, exemplary, then the dust-disease facts.
-- Death caused by the wrong, no dust disease: 50,000 up to death + 12,000 funeral = 62,000. Out: 80,000 non-economic,
-- 400,000 earnings after death, 10,000 loss from the death, 25,000 exemplary.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how much can the estate recover` TRUE FALSE 0 50000 80000 400000 10000 12000 25000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Mar 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS 62000
-- The same with the dust-disease rule met: 62,000 + 80,000 = 142,000.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how much can the estate recover` TRUE FALSE 0 50000 80000 400000 10000 12000 25000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `1 Mar 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS 142000
-- Dust disease, died 2005, determined before 7 November 2007: 62,000.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how much can the estate recover` TRUE FALSE 0 50000 80000 400000 10000 12000 25000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE `1 Jun 2005` TRUE `6 Nov 2007` EQUALS 62000
-- Death from an unrelated cause: 50,000 + 80,000 = 130,000; exemplary 25,000 out.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how much can the estate recover` FALSE FALSE 0 50000 80000 0 0 0 25000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Mar 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS 130000
-- Breach of promise to marry: only the 3,000 damage to the estate.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how much can the estate recover` FALSE TRUE 3000 50000 80000 0 0 0 25000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Mar 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS 3000
-- Breach of promise with no damage to the estate: nothing.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- how much can the estate recover` FALSE TRUE 0 50000 80000 0 0 0 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `1 Mar 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS 0

§ `s 7 -- the last day to take proceedings against the estate`

#ASSERT `s 7 -- by when must I take proceedings against the estate` FALSE `15 Mar 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7 -- by when must I take proceedings against the estate` TRUE `15 Mar 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS JUST `15 Mar 2025`
-- A grant on 29 February: 28 February next year (fork F6).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- by when must I take proceedings against the estate` TRUE `29 Feb 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` EQUALS JUST `28 Feb 2025`
-- The Supreme Court allowed a further period to 1 September 2025.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- by when must I take proceedings against the estate` TRUE `15 Mar 2024` TRUE `1 Sep 2025` EQUALS JUST `1 Sep 2025`
-- A "further period" ending before the 12 months would end does not shorten it (fork F8).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- by when must I take proceedings against the estate` TRUE `15 Mar 2024` TRUE `1 Jan 2025` EQUALS JUST `15 Mar 2025`

§ `s 7 -- can I take proceedings against the estate`

-- Arguments: kind, pending at death, arose on, died on, court finds it reasonable, granted, granted on, further period
-- allowed, further period ends on, taken, taken on, today.
-- A contract claim: s 7 sets no condition.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `CONTRACT` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` FALSE TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `NO S 7 CONDITION`
-- Proceedings pending at the death.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` TRUE `1 Jan 2020` `1 Jun 2024` FALSE TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `PENDING`
-- Arose exactly 12 months before the death ("not earlier than"), proceedings on the anniversary of the grant (edges);
-- a Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act claim, brought in by s 9(1).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `FATAL INJURIES` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` FALSE TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `15 Aug 2025` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `TAKEN IN TIME`
-- One day late.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` FALSE TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `16 Aug 2025` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- Arose one day more than 12 months before the death, court not satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `31 May 2023` `1 Jun 2024` FALSE TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `1 Feb 2025` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `AROSE TOO EARLY`
-- The same, court satisfied it is reasonable (s 7(2)); proceedings within the 12 months.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `31 May 2023` `1 Jun 2024` TRUE TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `1 Feb 2025` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `TAKEN IN TIME`
-- s 7(2) does not save proceedings taken after the 12 months.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `31 May 2023` `1 Jun 2024` TRUE TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `16 Aug 2025` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- No grant yet, nothing taken.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` FALSE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `NOT BEGUN`
-- No grant yet, proceedings already taken (fork F9).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` FALSE FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `1 Jul 2024` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `TAKEN IN TIME`
-- Proceedings taken before the grant (counted as day 0, fork F9).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` FALSE TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `1 Jul 2024` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `TAKEN IN TIME`
-- Not yet taken: today the last day, and the day after.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` FALSE TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` `15 Aug 2025` EQUALS `STILL IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` FALSE TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` `16 Aug 2025` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- A further period to 1 December 2025: the day before, the last day, and the day after.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` FALSE TRUE `15 Aug 2024` TRUE `1 Dec 2025` TRUE `30 Nov 2025` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `TAKEN IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` FALSE TRUE `15 Aug 2024` TRUE `1 Dec 2025` TRUE `1 Dec 2025` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `TAKEN IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `1 Jun 2023` `1 Jun 2024` FALSE TRUE `15 Aug 2024` TRUE `1 Dec 2025` TRUE `2 Dec 2025` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `OUT OF TIME`
-- Death on 29 February 2024: 12 months before is 28 February 2023 (fork F6).
#ASSERT `s 7 -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `28 Feb 2023` `29 Feb 2024` FALSE TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `1 Feb 2025` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `TAKEN IN TIME`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- can I take proceedings against the estate` `TORT` FALSE `27 Feb 2023` `29 Feb 2024` FALSE TRUE `15 Aug 2024` FALSE `1 Jan 2020` TRUE `1 Feb 2025` `7 Nov 2026` EQUALS `AROSE TOO EARLY`

§ `s 7(1)(b) -- the regulative rule alone`

-- 365 days allowed (15 August 2024 to 15 August 2025): day 0 and day 365 in time; day 366 late.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- taking proceedings on this day is in time` 365 0
#ASSERT `s 7 -- taking proceedings on this day is in time` 365 365
#ASSERT NOT (`s 7 -- taking proceedings on this day is in time` 365 366)
#ASSERT `the days from` `15 Aug 2024` `to` `15 Aug 2025` EQUALS 365
